{{Short description|Football tournament group stage}}
{{Use dmy dates|date=June 2018}}
'''Group 6''' was one of six groups of national teams competing in the First group stage of the [[1982 FIFA World Cup]]. Play began on 14 June and ended on 23 June 1982.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.rsssf.org/tables/82full.html |title=World Cup 1982 finals |publisher=[[RSSSF]] |access-date=30 April 2026}}</ref> The group consisted of four teams: Seeded team [[Brazil national football team|Brazil]], the [[Soviet Union national football team|Soviet Union]], [[Scotland national football team|Scotland]] and World Cup debutants [[New Zealand men's national football team|New Zealand]].<ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/spain1982/groups/ |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20180521170139/http://www.fifa.com/worldcup/archive/spain1982/groups/ |url-status=dead |archive-date=21 May 2018 |title=World Cup 1982 Spain » Groups |accessdate=3 May 2020 |work=FIFA.com}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://www.worldfootball.net/competition/ro9329/md0/results-and-standings/ |title=World Cup 1982 Spain » Group 6 |access-date=3 May 2020 |work=WorldFootball.net}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://books.google.com/books?id=ibqbuTkY8w0C&q=1982+FIFA+World+Cup+Group+6&pg=PA262 |title=World Cup 1982 Spain - Group 6 |accessdate=3 May 2020 |work=Google Books}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.planetworldcup.com/CUPS/1982/wc82index.html|title=World Cup 1982 |accessdate=3 May 2020 |work=Planet World Cup}}</ref>

Brazil won the group with three consecutive victories and advanced to the second round, along with the Soviet Union, who finished ahead of Scotland by virtue of goal difference.<ref>{{cite web|url=http://www.historicalkits.co.uk/international/tournaments/fifa-world-cup/1982/1982-group-6.html |title=1982 FIFA World Cup Group 6 |accessdate=3 May 2020 |work=Historical Football Kits}}</ref><ref>{{cite web|url=https://globalsportsarchive.com/competition/soccer/fifa-world-cup-1982-spain/group-stage/301/ |title=1982 FIFA World Cup Group 6 |accessdate=3 May 2020 |work=Global Sports Archive}}</ref>

